# Generated from: specs/197-move-write-spec-publication-lifecycle-into-code-while-keeping-native-plan/requirements.md
Feature: Move write-spec publication lifecycle into code while keeping native plan
  As a write-spec operator in the TUI
  I want issue discovery, approval publication, and continue-loop candidate filtering to run in existing publish helpers
  So that the model spends tokens on requirements and design, not git/gh lifecycle prose

  # --- Happy Path ---

  @SCN001
  Scenario: discovery returns complete deterministic input
    Given open issue N has no existing spec package
    When write-spec runs publish-approved-spec discover --issue N
    Then JSON contains issue metadata, feature-or-bug classification, derived slug, target directory, resolved spec status, and approval source
    And bug label selects bug while spike does not create a separate path
    And discovery reuses shared specStatus and resolveSpecDir rules
    And discovery performs no repository mutation

  @SCN002
  Scenario: approved native plan publishes through existing helpers
    Given the first issue plan contains full requirements, design, tasks, and Gherkin bodies
    When the operator approves the native plan
    Then execution runs prepare, writes four Approved files, runs commit-push, and runs merge in order
    And commit and PR title are docs: approve spec for #N
    And the PR body mentions #N without a closing keyword
    And successful merge leaves the issue open and the working tree on the default branch

  @SCN003
  Scenario: continue helper returns every eligible candidate
    Given the session has published issue numbers
    When write-spec runs candidates with repeated --published arguments
    Then the helper lists up to 100 open issues
    And it drops published numbers and shared-status Approved worktree, local-branch, and remote-branch packages
    And it returns every remaining number/title row sorted numerically
    And the workflow presents at most the first three rows plus Finished in a native ask

  # --- Alternative Paths ---

  @SCN004
  Scenario: existing unique spec directory wins over current title slug
    Given issue N has one unapproved specs/N-existing-slug directory
    When discover runs after the issue title changed
    Then targetDir is the existing directory
    And the package is revised in place after approval
    And no second leading-N directory is created

  @SCN005
  Scenario: continuation preserves plan and interview budgets
    Given one spec was already proposed and published in the session
    When the operator selects another candidate
    Then that issue receives a fresh maximum-three-ask interview budget
    And its local plan still contains all four full file bodies
    And no second xd propose is invoked

  # --- Error Handling ---

  @SCN006
  Scenario: discovery fails closed on unreadable input
    Given issue N is unreadable, malformed, number-mismatched, or missing state
    When discover runs
    Then it exits non-zero with reasonCode issue_unreadable
    And it does not create a branch or spec directory

  @SCN007
  Scenario: ambiguous approval status is never offered
    Given an issue has ambiguous leading-number directories or branch packages
    When discover or candidates evaluates that issue
    Then the shared resolver failure is returned
    And candidates does not include the issue as unapproved

  @SCN008
  Scenario: non-TUI write-spec remains unavailable
    Given print or RPC invokes sdlc-write-spec
    When the extension routes the command
    Then it prints Run /sdlc-write-spec in the TUI.
    And no commands/sdlc-write-spec.md surface exists

  @SCN009
  Scenario: Finished output remains exact
    Given at least one spec was published in the session
    When the operator selects Finished
    Then output lists Published specs with issue and branch names
    And the next line is Next step: /sdlc-execute #<first-published>
    And the working tree remains on the repository default branch
